hes following that cuff edge; the cuff's weave and its seam occupy the same exposed patch. Her bent elbows keep the hands close together over the supported hat, and her seated torso rests comfortably behind the surface. The nearer cuff, acting grip, needle eye, thread route and ribbon contact are spread within one clear plane with separate visible contours. The chair back and edge of the work surface retain enough form to identify the seated repair setting behind her. Side window light grazes the cuff and the silver needle, separating the yarn crossings and stitch row with small natural shadows. The hat remains supported at the lower frame, the face occupies the upper side, and the joined hands form the quiet visual center between them. Moderate depth of field keeps the eyes, complete acting hands, needle and cuff weave crisp together, while the existing place cue remains softly identifiable. Render the moment with restrained documentary intimacy, believable proportions, continuous fingers and wrists, realistic thread thickness, and the tactile clarity of an actual close photograph. A shared focus zone draws the recognizable face, the needle-gripping hand with its ribbon contact, and a softly legible chair and work-surface edge into one continuous reading.",
